## 3. Codebase Analysis & Strategic Guidance

The following analysis is based on my direct review of the current codebase. Use these notes and tips to guide your implementation.

### Relevant Existing Code
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/main.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Boots the Vue 3 admin SPA by creating the app, wiring Pinia, router, PrimeVue, Ripple, and ToastService, importing PrimeVue/PrimeIcons/theme CSS plus `@/assets/main.css`, and emitting a telemetry event (`app:hydrated`) once the root component mounts.
    *   **Recommendation:** When you expand the SPA you MUST keep this entry point minimal—register any global plugins/components (e.g., API clients, i18n) here rather than re-initializing elsewhere, and reuse the provided `emitTelemetryEvent` helper so future performance metrics remain consistent.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/router/index.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Declares Vue Router history with `/admin` base, wraps authenticated modules beneath `DefaultLayout`, lazy-loads views, and enforces guards for auth, vendor roles, RBAC, and feature flags using `useAuthStore`/`useTenantStore`; it also emits telemetry on every route change.
    *   **Recommendation:** Register new admin routes by extending this router file—set `meta.title`, `meta.requiresAuth`, and optional `meta.featureFlag/requiredRole` so the guards continue to work, and remember to add module route arrays via spread if you create dedicated route files.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/stores/catalog.ts`
    *   **Summary:** Pinia store stub managing catalog server state (products/categories caches, filters, pagination, optimistic selection) with computed helpers and placeholder async loaders meant to be replaced by real API calls.
    *   **Recommendation:** Implement real catalog fetching logic inside this store—reuse the cache map/Etag fields for conditional requests, honor filter arguments before hitting `/api/v1/admin/catalog` endpoints, and expose new actions for create/update so components stay thin.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/views/DashboardView.vue`
    *   **Summary:** Simple scaffold for the admin dashboard: renders KPI metric cards and an info alert using Tailwind utility classes plus shared base components.
    *   **Recommendation:** Flesh out dashboard widgets here by importing reusable cards/lists; keep the layout wrapper (`max-w-7xl mx-auto`) and leverage instrumentation IDs so future telemetry matches the UI/UX spec’s AdminDashboard organism.

### Implementation Tips & Notes
*   **Tip:** The SPA already emits telemetry via `emitTelemetryEvent`; when adding API integrations or new routes, dispatch additional events (e.g., `catalog:list:load`) from stores/components instead of `console.log` to align with the observability roadmap.
*   **Tip:** All protected navigation relies on `useAuthStore` and `useTenantStore`; hook JWT bootstrap + feature flags into those stores once backend auth endpoints are ready so you avoid duplicating tenant/role checks in individual components.
*   **Tip:** PrimeVue styling is globally configured for outlined inputs and Ripple; prefer PrimeVue data components (DataTable, Dialog, Toast) for catalog management, and import their CSS once at the view level to keep bundle size predictable.
*   **Tip:** Quinoa expects the admin web assets under `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui`; ensure any new dependencies are added to that package’s `package.json` and exposed via `vite.config.ts` so Maven builds remain deterministic.
*   **Note:** `tests/admin` already contains Cypress specs scaffolding POS/portal behaviors—extend those or add Vitest unit files alongside new stores/modules so CI coverage can gate regressions per the acceptance criteria.
*   **Warning:** Store stubs currently return mock data; until backend endpoints are functional, keep UI resilient (loading/empty/error states) and guard any destructive actions with feature flags so multi-tenant data safety assumptions from the blueprint hold.
EOF'
